1
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:03,600
晚安 三角形 晚安 正方形
Good night, Triangle. Good night, Square.

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:06,960
谢谢你们让我们看到学习有多么快乐
Thanks for showing us how fun it is to learn.

3
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:10,080
你能去拿下他们的睡衣 还是我...
Do you want to get their pajamas, or should I...

4
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:16,840
接下来播出《血腥杂交7: 器官囤积者的崛起》
Next, "Blood Orgy 7: Rise of the Organ Hoarder."

5
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:27,020
天啊
Oh, my God!

6
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:28,900
为什么
Why?!

7
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:29,200
为什么
Why?!

8
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:44,140
你是丹尼尔·布恩吗
Are you Daniel Boone?

9
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:46,700
你是谁
Who's asking?

10
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:50,481
我是来参观下肯塔基州的
I just came to see Kentucky,

11
00:00:50,481 --> 00:00:52,407
全国第五大烟草出产州
the fifth-largest tobacco producer

12
00:00:52,407 --> 00:00:55,839
和第三大产煤州
and the third-largest coal producer in the country.

13
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:58,240
我感觉身临其境
I feel like I am there.

14
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:00,620
唯一比儿童剧院更让人痛苦的
The only thing more painful than children's theater

15
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:02,580
就是我背部的疼痛
is what's going on with my back right now.

16
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:05,180
你为何不好好服用医生开给你的药
Why can't you take the pills that the doctor gave you

17
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:07,520
这样你就能享受你儿子的精彩表演了
so that you can enjoy your son's tour de force?

18
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:08,500
我只需要伸展一下身子
I just need a little stretch.

19
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:10,520
这年头 有点小毛病医生就给你开药
Doctors give you pills for everything today.

20
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:12,040
现在我们需要一位志愿者
Now we need a volunteer.

21
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:14,080
普里契特先生 谢谢你的热情参与
Mr. Pritchett, thank you for your enthusiasm.

22
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:14,620
什么
What?

23
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:17,180
我们的一位小演员被他继父绑架了
One of our players has been kidnapped by his stepfather,

24
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:18,260
但是演出必须进行下去
but the show must go on.

25
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:21,180
每当一块领土成为新的州 就在国旗上放颗星
Place a star on the flag every time a territory becomes a state.

26
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:22,575
说真的 但是警方...
Seriously, but do the police --

27
00:01:22,575 --> 00:01:27,260
来点掌声怎么样
How 'bout a round of applause?!

28
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:30,120
快点 观众快要失去兴趣了
Faster, please. We're losing them.

29
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:30,920
你在哪儿呢
Where are you?

30
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:34,380
你要错过乔的《美国团结50州》演出了
You're missing Joe's tribute to the 50 nifty United States.

31
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:37,820
我在家躺在床上呢 重感冒
I'm at home in bed with the worst cold.

32
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:39,420
恐怕我们全家都中招倒下了
Afraid the whole family's down.

33
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:42,000
恐怕有几棵绿植都倒下了
Might've even lost a few house plants, yeah.

34
00:01:42,223 --> 00:01:44,307
好了 我得休息了
Okay, well, I'm gonna get some rest now.

35
00:01:44,307 --> 00:01:45,492
好的 保重
Alright. Take care.

36
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:51,797
菲尔
Phil!

37
00:01:51,797 --> 00:01:55,400
你跟我说你把你爸的房车卖掉了
You told me you sold your dad's RV!

38
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,600
你还跟我说你要跑5英里呢
And you told me you were running your 5-mile loop!

39
00:01:57,933 --> 00:01:59,961
这条街在你3英里跑步路线上
This street is on your 3-mile course,

40
00:01:59,961 --> 00:02:02,208
所以你到底是在生谁的气呢 克莱尔
so who are you really mad at, Claire?

41
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:05,040
歌洛莉亚 我们很抱歉
Gloria, we are so sorry,

42
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:07,200
但我们没办法去看小乔的演出了
but we're not gonna be able to make it to Joe's play.

43
00:02:07,359 --> 00:02:09,820
不 是因为罗纳多的妈妈 她...
No, no, Ronaldo's mom, she had --

44
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:11,360
她做了个紧急手术
well, she had emergency surgery,

45
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:14,520
他和胡娇把他们的大丹犬放到我们家寄养了
and, uh, he and Pepper dropped off their Great Danes

46
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:16,160
事先完全没通知
to our place with no warning.

47
00:02:17,318 --> 00:02:19,863
不 别碰那个 千万别碰花瓶
No! No, stay away from that! Not the vase!

48
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,840
抱歉 歌洛莉亚 我得先挂了
Sorry, Gloria. I gotta go.

49
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:25,400
你就不能用患感冒当借口吗
You couldn't just say you had a cold?

50
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:27,139
是啊 亚伯拉罕·林肯
Oh, yeah, and Abe Lincoln,

51
00:02:27,139 --> 00:02:29,098
他可以简单地说"87年前"
he could've said, "87 years ago,"

52
00:02:29,098 --> 00:02:31,140
哈姆雷特也可以说"不如我自杀算了"
and Hamlet could've said, "Maybe I'll kill myself."

53
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:33,020
不行 最后的那场收尾戏
No, it's the finishing touches

54
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:35,574
才是决定作品超凡脱俗的关键 米奇尔
that separate the merely good from great, Mitchell!

55
00:02:35,574 --> 00:02:38,180
亲爱的 我知道你对这事很紧张...
Sweetie, I know you're really tense about this --

56
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:39,801
别 别说 别乱说招致霉运
No, no, no! Don't jinx it, don't jinx it!

57
00:02:39,801 --> 00:02:42,928
-小卡要去那个大学当主教练... -打住 打住
- Cam is up for head coach at the University of Nor-- - Bup, bup, bup!

58
00:02:44,692 --> 00:02:45,494
打住 打住
Bup, bup!

59
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,900
小卡有可能去中北部密苏里学院
Cam is up for head football coach

60
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:50,080
当橄榄球主教练
at the University of North Central Missouri.

61
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,460
那是他梦想的工作
It's his dream job,

62
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:53,320
他们今天会打电话给他告知结果
and they're supposed to call him about it today,

63
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:55,360
这让他有点疯狂
and it's making him a little crazy.

64
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:56,354
实际上...
In f-fact --

65
00:02:56,354 --> 00:02:58,371
克莱尔向来都是我爸最爱的孩子
C-Claire's always Dad's favorite,

66
00:02:58,371 --> 00:03:00,100
我对此真的很气愤
and I-I'm really miffed about that.

67
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:01,920
天啊 又在说这破事啊
Oh, boy. This again, huh?

68
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:04,280
好了 继续说
Okay. No, go on.

69
00:03:04,620 --> 00:03:06,459
-我准备好了 -我的老天
- I'm ready. - Oh, my God!

70
00:03:06,459 --> 00:03:09,080
-亲爱的 你好美 看看她 -小宝贝
- Honey, you look gorgeous! Look at her. - Ah, sweetie!

71
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:11,180
我能根据我的初次约会给你点建议吗
Now, may I give you a piece of advice from my first date?

72
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:13,140
别说你有多想要孩子
Don't say how much you want to have kids,

73
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:15,000
别哭 你的妆会花掉的
and don't cry, because your makeup will run.

74
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:17,900
我更担心我的约会对象看到你们俩会夺路而逃
I'm more worried about my date running when he sees you two there.

75
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:19,819
你们不会注意到我们的存在 好吗
You'll barely even notice us, okay?

76
00:03:19,819 --> 00:03:22,380
做你真实的自我就好 你很风趣幽默的
Just be yourself. You are -- You're so funny.

77
00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:24,080
你可以跟他说那个有趣的故事
Okay, tell that funny story

78
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:26,160
就是一个老醉汉亲吻驴子的那个
of the old drunk guy who was kissing the donkey.

79
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:27,920
干嘛扯我家 你的家人就很完美吗
Oh, because your family's perfect?

80
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:30,340
好了 天啊 来了来了
Okay. Oh, my God! That's it!

81
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:31,100
工作那边打来的
That's the job!

82
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:32,859
我的手机在哪儿 我的手机在哪儿
Where's my phone?! Where's my phone?!

83
00:03:32,859 --> 00:03:35,002
这简直是最糟糕的事...
This is the worst thing that could be happ--

84
00:03:35,292 --> 00:03:37,085
好吧 只是我的冥想程序而已
Okay, it's just my mediation app.

85
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:42,620
好了 你得控制下你男人
Okay, you need to control your man.

86
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:44,120
如果他今晚收到的是坏消息
If he gets bad news tonight

87
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,459
然后在兰迪面前崩溃了
and melts down in front of Randy,

88
00:03:45,459 --> 00:03:48,530
我就可以跟与他吻别这件事"吻别"了
I can kiss "kssing him goodbye" goodbye.

89
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:50,371
没事的 有我在呢 我们走吧
Okay, no, I gotcha, I gotcha. Come on, let's go.

90
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:53,041
我理解我们都会对我们父母的东西
I understand we all get attached to things

91
00:03:53,041 --> 00:03:54,340
有深深的依恋感 不舍得处理掉
that belonged to our parents.

92
00:03:54,340 --> 00:03:55,160
不是这原因
That's not it.

93
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:57,520
我这么做是为了让你跟我享受一些冒险旅程
I'm doing this so you and I can have some adventures.

94
00:03:57,620 --> 00:03:59,500
难道你看不到 当我们驾车驶过金门大桥时
Can't you see yourself making lists and folding shirts

95
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:01,140
你在列清单 叠衣服的画面吗
while we drive across the Golden Gate Bridge?

96
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:03,240
我们永远不会用上这车的
We're never gonna use this thing.

97
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:05,760
耗油太狠 找个停车的地方要一小时
It guzzles gas, and it takes an hour to park.

98
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:06,780
那就停在这里吧
Well, then leave it here.

99
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:07,940
你多年来一直想要一间客房啊
You've always wanted a guest house.

100
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:10,560
我不要餐桌上还有安全带的客房
Not one with seat belts at the dining table.

101
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:14,360
没得商量 迪兰
No discussion, Dylan.

102
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:16,140
我们要带他们去看婴儿心理医生
We're taking them to see a baby psychiatrist.

103
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:18,320
你还是在纠结那部疯电影吗
Are you still talking about that crazy movie?

104
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:19,900
孩子的纯洁心灵被毁了
Well, it messed them up!

105
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:21,300
我们带他们去了公园
We took them to the park.

106
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,913
玩秋千 他们觉得无聊
Swing set -- bored.

107
00:04:22,913 --> 00:04:24,140
看萌萌小松鼠 他们打鼾
Cute squirrels -- snore.

108
00:04:24,140 --> 00:04:25,778
然后有个老太太在遛狗
Then an old lady walking her poodle

109
00:04:25,778 --> 00:04:27,560
绊了一跤 被拖着从玫瑰花丛里穿过
trips and gets dragged through a rosebush,

110
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:29,040
这两个孩子竟然笑出声
and these two burst out laughing

111
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,440
就像两个玩挠痒痒大战的神经病
like two stoners in a tickle fight.

112
00:04:30,540 --> 00:04:31,980
你们肯定只是反应过度啦
I'm sure you're both overreacting

113
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:33,420
所有新手爸妈都会这样
the way all new parents do.

114
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,040
不 妈妈 我们要把小孩养坏了
No, Mom, we're screwing this up.

115
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:36,580
我们最少也需要寻求些帮助
At the very least, we need help,

116
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:38,280
比如互惠生[一对]保姆之类的
like -- like an au pair or something.

117
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:39,380
那是两个保姆的意思 对吗
That's two nannies, right?

118
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:40,380
-正确 -好
- Correct. - Okay.

119
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:45,317
你们看 他们对那只蝴蝶多温柔呀
Look at how gentle they're being with that butterfly.

120
00:04:45,317 --> 00:04:47,864
看见没 你们只是瞎操心...
See? You two were worrying for no--

121
00:04:47,887 --> 00:04:49,820
-他们把蝴蝶撕碎了 -天啊
- They're tearing it apart. Ohh! - Oh God!

122
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:52,040
这样好不好 我们把孩子们交给亲家母
What do you say we leave the babies with Farrah

123
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:54,340
我们几个大人出去边吃晚饭边商量这事
and the grown-ups go out and talk about this over dinner?

124
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:55,220
好主意
Great idea.

125
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:57,320
可是有四个人耶
Oh! Four people, though.

126
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:58,900
普通轿车坐不下呢
Try fitting that in a regular car.

127
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:00,012
等一下
Wait a minute.

128
00:05:00,012 --> 00:05:04,200
要是我们开那辆房... 你逗我呢吗
What if we took the R-- you kidding me?!

129
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,820
提醒我买些车轮锁啊
Remind me to buy some wheel blocks!

130
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:11,100
天啊 莉莉需要我帮她一把
Oh, God. Lily needs my help.

131
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:14,920
你这是在演哪一出
What the hell are you doing?

132
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:17,078
我提醒她分享那个好笑的驴子故事
I'm -- I'm trying to get her to tell that funny donkey story.

133
00:05:17,078 --> 00:05:18,540
你就学《小熊维尼》里的屹耳驴叫吗
By making an Eeyore sound?

134
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:20,640
知道吗 不是所有驴子都那么丧的
You know what? Not all donkeys are depressed.

135
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:22,200
这刻板印象真没礼貌
That's an offensive stereotype

136
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:24,840
都是一群无知爱荷华州人传的谣言
perpetuated by a bunch of ignorant Iowans.

137
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:26,160
天啊 我的手机震了
Oh, my God! My phone's buzzing!

138
00:05:26,685 --> 00:05:27,649
原来只是朗吉尼斯
It's just Longinus.

139
00:05:27,649 --> 00:05:30,780
知道了啦 你在网红汉堡店遇到演员玛丽·奥斯蒙了
Yeah, we know. You met Marie Osmond at a Five Guys.

140
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:31,680
谁在乎啊
Nobody cares.

141
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:32,860
打住
Stop!

142
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:34,938
我朋友说我们该尝尝这里的土豆
My friend said we should try the potato.

143
00:05:34,938 --> 00:05:37,345
-莉莉 -同志们 同志们 同志们
- Lily! - Hey, guys. Guys, guys, guys, guys, guys, guys, guys.

144
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,320
你们好啊 你们怎么来了
Hey, guys! What are you doing here?

145
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:41,027
休息一下 暂时先不给我们孩子留下童年阴影了
Oh, just taking a break from scarring our children.

146
00:05:41,027 --> 00:05:42,180
别夸张了
Now, come on.

147
00:05:42,180 --> 00:05:43,820
海莉和迪兰有点小崩溃
Haley and Dylan were having a little bit of a meltdown,

148
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,902
我们想着土豆屋不是快停业了吗
and we thought we'd hit Spuds one last time

149
00:05:45,902 --> 00:05:46,860
就抓紧来吃最后一次
before they close for good.

150
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:48,200
就是啊 真伤感不是吗
I know. It's sad, isn't it?

151
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:50,199
-我们小时候每年生日都是在这过的 -是啊
- Remember we used to spend all of our birthdays here... - Yeah!

152
00:05:50,199 --> 00:05:53,300
-土豆宝宝霍利会唱给给我们听 -对
- ...and Spuddy Holly would always sing to us. - Yes! Oh.

153
00:05:53,459 --> 00:05:56,020
♪ 加扇贝 去油炸 裹上洋葱 ♪
♪ Scalloped, fried, or lyonnaise ♪

154
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:57,800
♪ 土豆屋的土豆好吃疯 ♪
♪ Spuds' potatoes amaze ♪

155
00:05:57,920 --> 00:05:58,700
♪ 生日快乐 ♪
♪ Happy birthday ♪

156
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:00,620
我想强调一下 我只是被收养的
I want to stress that I'm adopted.

157
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:02,480
我们要不别打扰那对小情人约会了吧
Why don't we leave the lovebirds to their date?

158
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:03,840
好主意 但你们知道吗
Good idea, but you know what?

159
00:06:04,060 --> 00:06:06,341
越多人一起分享土豆越美味哦 和坐车一样
Spuds is better with more people, much like a vehicle.

160
00:06:06,341 --> 00:06:08,542
看看他们能否安排我们坐一块吧
Let's -- Let's see if they can sit the rest of us together.

161
00:06:08,542 --> 00:06:09,204
-好啊 -行
- Okay, yeah. - Okay.

162
00:06:09,204 --> 00:06:09,946
好
Alright.

163
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:17,960
我关注了和小卡竞争教练职位的
I'd been following Cam's competitor for the coaching spot

164
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:19,160
那人的图享网账号
on Instagram, and --

165
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:21,580
他打败小卡得到了那份工作
...he beat Cam out for the job,

166
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:22,960
这代表
which meant, any minute,

167
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:25,120
小卡随时会得知这令人心碎的消息
Cam would be getting the devastating news himself.

168
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:28,060
我不能指望靠土豆屋的欢乐气氛
And I-I-I couldn't rely on the joyful environment of Spuds

169
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:29,020
来缓解这一冲击
to cushion the blow.

170
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:32,020
但这餐厅有个美名 名主持拉里·金在这
Although, it is famously where Larry King broke up

171
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:32,940
和四任老婆分的手
with four of his wives.

172
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:34,729
小卡 小卡
Cam. Cam.

173
00:06:34,729 --> 00:06:36,640
我刚得知一个坏消息
I-I-I just got some bad news,

174
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:38,420
我想最好是由我来告诉你
and I think it's best that you hear it from me.

175
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:39,180
我听说了
Oh, I heard.

176
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:40,818
逆天土豆居然卖光了
They're out of the Impossible Potato.

177
00:06:40,818 --> 00:06:41,892
不好意思
Now, I'm sorry,

178
00:06:41,892 --> 00:06:45,238
你们既然吹嘘这是史上第一款纯肉做的土豆
you advertise the first potato made entirely of meat,

179
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:47,868
最好就备够所有人的量啊
ya better have enough for everyone.

180
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,600
求你了 快吃药吧
Please just take those pills.

181
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:55,240
你现在比参加路易斯安那购地案的叛徒
You're more crooked than General James Wilkinson

182
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,960
詹姆斯·威尔金森还坐立不安
during the Louisiana Purchase.

183
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:58,960
只剩下最后一个州了
We're down to the last state.

184
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:00,770
我动一下还比较舒服
It's actually better if I move.

185
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:05,580
这里太美了
Wow. This is gorgeous.

186
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:07,640
这地方叫什么来着
What do you call this place, again?

187
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:08,920
珍珠港
Pearl Harbor.

188
00:07:17,358 --> 00:07:19,458
扶好国旗 兄弟们
Save the flag, boys!

189
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:30,100
海莉 别玩手机了
Haley, get off your phone.

190
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:31,640
有迪兰妈妈在 他们没事的
The babies are fine with Dylan's mom.

191
00:07:31,820 --> 00:07:34,080
如果你觉得紧张 房车里有我爸的旧足浴盆哦
If you're feeling tense, my dad's old foot bath is in the RV.

192
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,577
就插在车载打火机上
Plugs right into the cigarette lighter.

193
00:07:35,577 --> 00:07:37,200
老公 就算车里有座喷钱的山
Honey, there could be a money volcano

194
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:39,480
插在白葡萄酒喷泉里
that plugs right into a white wine fountain in there.

195
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:40,420
我还是不想要那破车
I still wouldn't want it.

196
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:42,140
我一直想起有些事忘记告诉她了
I keep remembering things I forgot to tell her.

197
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:43,180
我的小孩已经是反社会了
My kids are already sociopaths.

198
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:45,619
我不希望他们还因为吃草莓犯过敏
I don't need to give them a strawberry allergy on top of it.

199
00:07:45,619 --> 00:07:47,251
我非常十分完全理解你
Oh, I completely, totally get that.

200
00:07:47,251 --> 00:07:48,440
我要把你电话关了
Just gonna turn this off.

201
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:48,840
不如这样吧
You know what?

202
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:51,160
我们都把手机关掉 快点
Hey, let-- let's all turn off our phones. Come on.

203
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:53,140
-不要 -来嘛 享受当下
- Yeah, you can -- - No, come on. Live in the moment.

204
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:55,500
此刻多美好啊 我们和家人好友
I mean, appreciate the fact that we live in a town

205
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:57,180
住在同一个城市
with family and friends

206
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:58,940
齐聚一堂 这还是...
all sitting at the same table where --

207
00:07:58,940 --> 00:08:01,891
"前总统艾森豪威尔策划诺曼底登陆日入侵"的桌子
oh, yeah, "Eisenhower planned the D-Day invasion."

208
00:08:01,891 --> 00:08:03,120
这八成是假的吧
Well, that's probably not true.

209
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:04,400
听起来有人为可能要
Sounds like somebody's nervous

210
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,888
搬去密苏里州感到紧张
about a possible move to Missouri.

211
00:08:05,888 --> 00:08:07,440
不 我只是想指出
No, I'm -- I'm just pointing out

212
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:09,640
这里有很多很棒的人事物
that there are a lot of really great things here.

213
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:11,140
比如那段萌芽时期的恋情
Like -- Like, wouldn't it be a shame

214
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:13,080
如果提前结束了 那多可惜啊
to cut that blossoming relationship short?

215
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:15,780
说真的 我不太信任那个叫兰迪的
Actually, I'm not so sure how much I trust that Randy guy.

216
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:18,060
什么样的变态才会喜欢12岁小女孩啊
I mean, what kind of sicko is attracted to a 12-year-old?

217
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:20,020
不知道他父母是不是也教坏他了
I wonder if his parents messed him up, too.

218
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:21,160
我在一个妈咪博客上看到
You know, I read on a mommy blog

219
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:23,577
父母失职和孩子日后犯罪有直接联系
that bad parenting is a direct link to future criminality --

220
00:08:23,577 --> 00:08:24,900
还有当DJ
and deejaying.

221
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:25,440
好了 听我说
Okay, you know what?

222
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:26,480
你们得当心点
You two need to be careful

223
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:29,000
你们把时间都花在看育儿文章上
because you can read so much about how to parent,

224
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:30,940
也许会错过真正教养孩子的机会
you miss out on being one.

225
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:32,360
米奇尔就曾犯过这种错误
Mitchell struggled with that.

226
00:08:33,620 --> 00:08:34,409
放轻松
Just relax.

227
00:08:34,409 --> 00:08:36,016
小甜心
Aww, sweetheart.

228
00:08:36,909 --> 00:08:39,260
-你给她喷了发胶吗 -一点点
- Did you put hair spray in this? - Just a little bit, yes.

229
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:40,080
我来放点音乐
I'm gonna put some music on.

230
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,760
-不 小卡 我还要去上班 -跟她跳跳舞
- No, Cam, I have to go work. - Dance with her!

231
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:43,400
-别 没时间了 -一起摇摆吧
- Come on. I don't have time for this. - Put a little boogie in it.

232
00:08:43,471 --> 00:08:45,053
饶了我吧
No, come on, it--

233
00:08:45,053 --> 00:08:46,796
跳吧 你知道这首歌是你的菜
Just dance. You know you love this song.

234
00:08:46,947 --> 00:08:48,067
那好吧 好吧
Alright. Okay.

235
00:08:48,741 --> 00:08:50,414
谁才是舞后
Who's the dancing queen, huh?

236
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:54,180
一起摇摆吧
Put a little boogie in it.

237
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:56,060
看 好玩吧 是不是
See? Fun.

238
00:08:56,630 --> 00:08:58,260
妈呀 撞到她的头了吗
Oh, my -- was that her head?

239
00:08:58,260 --> 00:09:00,200
抱歉 我忘了故事最后是这样的
Sorry. I forgot how that story ended.

240
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:02,380
最后是我们在急诊室
It ended with us in the ER

241
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:04,640
那是全世界最好的医院之一
of one of the best hospitals in the world.

242
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:06,360
距离我们才不到两公里 多好
Nice having that only a mile away.

243
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:08,539
告诉你 布密苏里的平均寿命
I'll have you know that the life expectancy in Missouri

244
00:09:08,539 --> 00:09:10,880
刚刚超过了阿肯色州和关岛
just climbed above Arkansas and Guam.

245
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:12,600
把手机还给我 我要订购婴儿头盔
Okay, give me back my phone. I'm ordering baby helmets.

246
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:13,380
别再担心了
Stop worrying.

247
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:15,480
孩子们总是磕磕碰碰的
Kids get bonked all the time.

248
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:17,980
你知道卢克栽过多少跟头吗
Do you know how many tumbles Luke took?

249
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:21,580
他应该是想出去
I think he wants to go out.

250
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:22,780
好孩子
Good boy!

251
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:24,760
聪明的狗狗
Smart dog.

252
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:27,100
不想扫你的兴 不过这招所有狗都会吧
I hate to break it to you, but I think all dogs can do that.

253
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:28,840
我要出去玩
I'm gonna play outside.

254
00:09:33,420 --> 00:09:34,300
怎么回事啊
What happened?

255
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:35,880
他不也很好
And he's fine.

256
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:37,100
还好
...ish.

257
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:38,300
我喜欢卢克
I love the guy,

258
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:39,920
但我们对孩子的期望比他要高一些
but we're aiming a little bit higher than Luke.

259
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:42,360
海莉 其实孩子们偶尔受点小伤是好事
Haley, you kind of want your kids to get knocked around a little.

260
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:43,400
能让他们更坚强地
It toughens them up for things

261
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:44,720
面对成年人都会经历的事
that we all go through in adulthood.

262
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:46,300
老爸赢了
Daddy wins!

263
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:47,612
相信奇迹吗
Do you believe in miracles?!

264
00:09:47,612 --> 00:09:51,300
美利坚万岁 美利
Usa! Us--

265
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:51,978
不
Oh, no!

266
00:09:51,978 --> 00:09:52,960
上帝啊
Oh, geez!

267
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,340
天啊 刚刚那是什么
Oh, my -- What was that?

268
00:09:56,340 --> 00:09:57,580
-是个人吗 -我没事
- Was that a person that fell -- - I'm good!

269
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:57,900
爸爸
Dad?!

270
00:09:57,900 --> 00:10:00,660
老爸 接招
Hey, Dad, think fast.

271
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:02,980
你是不是有点儿过于
Aren't you being a little --

272
00:10:06,507 --> 00:10:09,004
哪有什么不测
But this isn't an emergen--

273
00:10:12,473 --> 00:10:14,722
现在有了
Now it I-I-I-I-is!

274
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:17,020
确实 我已经尝不出咸味了 不过
I mean, sure, I can no longer taste salt, but --

275
00:10:17,020 --> 00:10:18,900
我知道他们会有磕磕碰碰
I know that they're going to get bumps and bruises,

276
00:10:18,980 --> 00:10:21,580
但我指的是心灵创伤
but I'm talking about psychological scars.

277
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:23,440
我自己就有过那种经历
I've had some experience with that myself.

278
00:10:23,876 --> 00:10:26,600
惊喜啊啊啊
Surpri--

279
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:27,040
不
No!

280
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:28,060
不 不
No! No!

281
00:10:28,700 --> 00:10:29,680
对不起
I'm sorry!

282
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:30,760
什么都没发生
Nothing's happening!

283
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:31,740
我的天啊
Oh, my God!

284
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:33,340
她至今仍很受伤
It still haunts her.

285
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:35,320
听了别尴尬 不过她至今
Not to be weird, but she still won't let me

286
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:37,112
都不让我在做爱时提你们的名字
mention your names while we're making love.

287
00:10:37,112 --> 00:10:38,120
好吧
Okay.

288
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:40,000
瞧瞧啊
Well, well, well.

289
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:43,120
是的 瞧瞧啊
Yes, well, well, well.

290
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,340
看来你的感冒好多了
I see your cold is better.

291
00:10:45,418 --> 00:10:48,000
后来发现我只是有一点过敏啦
Turns out it was, like, an allergy...thing.

292
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,923
胡娇的大丹狗呢
And Pepper's Great Danes?

293
00:10:49,923 --> 00:10:51,345
你知道 它们是大型犬
Oh, uh, well, you know, they're big dogs.

294
00:10:51,345 --> 00:10:53,220
它们没有那么长的寿命
They -- Um, and they don't, uh, uh, live long.

295
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:54,105
所以它们
So they're --

296
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:56,420
它们死了
they're dead.

297
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:58,860
你一定以为我是弗雷德里克·苏厄德
I must look like Frederick Seward

298
00:10:58,860 --> 00:11:00,680
在收购阿拉斯加
during the Alaska Purchase,

299
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:03,780
显然你以为你怎么忽悠我都会买单
because, apparently, you think that I'll buy anything.

300
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,179
歌洛莉亚 好吧
Gloria, okay, okay.

301
00:11:05,179 --> 00:11:07,140
抱歉 抱歉我们对你说谎了
We're s-we're sorry-we're sorry we lied to you,

302
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:08,760
但假如这能让你感觉好些
but if it makes you feel any better,

303
00:11:09,180 --> 00:11:11,020
朗吉尼斯给你拍了一张很美的照片
Longinus took this really great photo of you

304
00:11:11,020 --> 00:11:12,480
就是你去夏奇拉演唱会那晚
at the Shakira concert the night

305
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:14,500
你得了红眼病不能去莉莉的单簧管独奏会
that you missed Lily's clarinet recital because of pink eye.

306
00:11:16,580 --> 00:11:20,340
看来你一直在等着对我会心一击
I see that you've been waiting to spring that attack on me,

307
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:23,380
像新奥尔良战役中的安德鲁·杰克逊那样
just like Andrew Jackson in the Battle of New Orleans.

308
00:11:23,460 --> 00:11:24,558
我得一直听她这么说话了吗
Is this my life now?

309
00:11:24,558 --> 00:11:25,876
我去趟卫生间
I'm gonna use the restroom.

310
00:11:25,876 --> 00:11:28,460
你们赶紧点个桌边烤土豆
Will someone order the table-side baked potatoes?

311
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:30,520
来这吃的一半原因就是为了看烤土豆表演
I mean, that's half of why you come here -- for the show.

312
00:11:32,260 --> 00:11:33,500
公共厕所
Public restroom, huh?

313
00:11:34,340 --> 00:11:36,240
真可惜他不能去自己车里解决私人问题
Shame he can't go in the privacy of his own car.

314
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:39,120
确实 房车里确实有卫生间
It's true. The RV does have a bathroom.

315
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:40,727
还有嵌死的咖啡机
And a bolted-down Mr. Coffee,

316
00:11:40,727 --> 00:11:42,813
防熊的底盘食品箱
bear-proof undercarriage food bins.

317
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:44,980
你觉得车已经跑过多少公里了
And how many miles would you say is on it?

318
00:11:45,460 --> 00:11:45,860
等等
Wait!

319
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,560
你居然要把她在同城网站上卖掉
You're selling her on Craigslist?

320
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:50,180
甚至用的照片还很难看
And this isn't even a good picture!

321
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:52,000
她这一面不上相
This is her bad side!

322
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:54,040
我懂房车的价值 克莱尔
Hey, look, I get the value of an RV, Claire.

323
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:57,680
加州有那么多自然美景值得探索
There is so much natural beauty to explore here in California.

324
00:11:57,820 --> 00:11:58,920
黄金之州
The Golden State!

325
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:01,180
你不是真的想反悔搬去密苏里吧
Are you really trying to get out of moving to Missouri?

326
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:02,060
不是
No, no!

327
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:05,958
听起来我们需要密苏里妥协案
Sounds like what we need is a Missouri Compromise.

328
00:12:05,958 --> 00:12:08,820
歌洛莉亚 你在给外公的土豆蒂尼下药吗
Gloria, are you drugging Grandpa's Potato-tini?

329
00:12:08,820 --> 00:12:11,140
你也看到他腰都直不起来了
You saw how bent over he is.

330
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:13,060
不知道为什么 他很怕吃药
For some reason, he's scared of pills,

331
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:15,020
我不能再看着他疼下去了
and I can't watch him suffer anymore.

332
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:17,860
我真讨厌餐厅用可爱的卫生间标识
I hate it when they get cute with the bathroom signs.

333
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:20,160
为什么薯条代表女士
Why would French fries mean ladies

334
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:21,260
烤土豆代表男士
and baked potato gents?

335
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:23,260
给其中一个小人加条裙子不就得了
Just throw one of them into a skirt.

336
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:24,740
爸
So, uh, Dad,

337
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:27,799
歌洛莉亚说你不肯吃背痛药
Gloria says that you won't take pills for your back?

338
00:12:27,799 --> 00:12:29,663
现在人人都要说我了吗
I got to get this from all sides now?

339
00:12:30,065 --> 00:12:32,320
我不喜欢那些药给我的影响 行吗
I don't like what they do to me, alright?

340
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:34,720
它们让我觉得特别
They make me feel super...

341
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:36,120
饥渴 便秘
Horny? Constipated?

342
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:37,640
情绪化
Emotional.

343
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:40,540
有时你忍一忍就过去了 但这次要命了
You know, sometimes you can just ride out a pause, buddy.

344
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:43,340
实在是太痛 我忍不住了
Anyway, the pain got so bad, I broke down.

345
00:12:43,380 --> 00:12:44,620
就在卫生间吃了两片药
I took a couple in the men's room,

346
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:47,100
已经到了最大剂量 所以准备好啦
which is the maximum dose, so strap in.

347
00:12:47,144 --> 00:12:48,408
不
N-n--

348
00:12:49,780 --> 00:12:51,240
我会怀念这个地方的
You know, I'm gonna miss this place.

349
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:53,580
看 土豆宝宝霍利
Look, Spuddy Holly!

350
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:56,017
他就要唱这些了 对吧
He just about said it all, didn't he?

351
00:12:56,017 --> 00:12:58,821
♪ 加扇贝 去油炸 裹上洋葱 ♪
♪ Scalloped, fried, lyonnaise. ♪

352
00:12:58,843 --> 00:13:01,093
♪ 土豆屋的土豆好吃疯 ♪
♪ Spuds' potatoes amaze ♪

353
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:04,800
四片 他没事吧
Four pills? Is he gonna be okay?

354
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:05,960
他没事的
He can handle it.

355
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:07,920
爸爸可是从八十年代的衣柜界活下来了
Dad lived through the closet scene in the '80s.

356
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:08,779
我也是
So did I.

357
00:13:08,779 --> 00:13:11,953
天啊 他在和莉莉和迪兰说话
Oh, my God. He's talking to Lily and Dylan!

358
00:13:12,797 --> 00:13:14,039
我才是迪兰
I'm Dylan.

359
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:16,900
兰迪 你让我想起了年轻时的我
You know, Randy, you remind me of a young me,

360
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:19,353
和一位越南美女在胡志明市游荡
prowling Saigon with a Vietnamese beauty.

361
00:13:19,353 --> 00:13:21,340
-我常去一个酒吧 -我们走吧
- There was this one bar I used to -- - Let's go.

362
00:13:21,340 --> 00:13:22,857
给你弄点黑咖啡喝
Let's get you some black coffee.

363
00:13:22,857 --> 00:13:25,860
躲猫猫啦 乔治 茵素
Peekaboo! George! Poppy!

364
00:13:25,860 --> 00:13:27,840
有人在家吗
Hello? Is anybody home?

365
00:13:29,534 --> 00:13:32,060
怎么回事 纸巾先生通常都能逗笑他们啊
What gives? Mister Napkin usually kills.

366
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:32,921
谁要咖啡
Who wanted coffee?

367
00:13:32,921 --> 00:13:33,714
这
Ah, here!

368
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,617
他们笑了 看到吗 他们有病
They're laughing! See? They're psychos!

369
00:13:37,617 --> 00:13:40,780
对不起 先生 你还好吗
Ay! Sorry, mister. Are you okay?

370
00:13:40,780 --> 00:13:43,780
我没一点感觉 更吓人了
I actually don't feel anything, which is even more scary.

371
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,800
去感觉 别害怕 小家伙
Don't be scared to feel, buddy.

372
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:47,460
你最后可能会逃离
You could end up running away

373
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:49,780
你孩子的情绪发作
from an emotional situation with your kids,

374
00:13:49,780 --> 00:13:52,840
但解开孩子情绪的结是最值的
and those are always the most rewarding.

375
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,340
要我说 你很幸运
You ask me, you're lucky.

376
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:55,860
她发短信甩我的
She dumped me by text

377
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:57,440
当时还在和她年长的男友热吻
while making out with her old boyfriend.

378
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:59,260
我崩溃哭泣
I broke down crying.

379
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:01,300
炭笔条花得跟睫毛膏一样
My charcoal ran like mascara.

380
00:14:01,860 --> 00:14:04,200
还得靠另一队的吉利物安慰我来着
I had to be comforted by the other team's mascot.

381
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:05,012
这是幸运吗
Lucky?

382
00:14:05,012 --> 00:14:07,120
我不会骗你
Aw, I'm not gonna lie to you.

383
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:07,940
这很糟糕
It sucks,

384
00:14:07,940 --> 00:14:11,086
有时候糟糕的感觉还会持续一阵子
and sometimes it's got to suck for a while.

385
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:13,300
我真希望我可以说出什么咒语
I just wish I could say some magic words

386
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:15,160
或是拥抱你 就让这感觉烟消云散
or give you a hug, make it all go away.

387
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:20,540
某种程度上 是他培育我成长
In a way, he raised me.

388
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:23,120
你振作点行不行啊 老爸
Pull yourself together, man!

389
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:24,820
海莉
Haley, um,

390
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:28,680
我想你药物导致变正常人的外公
I think what your... chemically humanized grandfather

391
00:14:28,820 --> 00:14:30,700
想说的是 孩子天生就是生存者
is trying to say is that kids are built to last.

392
00:14:30,889 --> 00:14:32,560
的确 他们会碰到许多磨难
Sure, they -- they go through stuff,

393
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:34,520
但雨过就会天晴 特别是有你们在身边帮忙
but they survive, especially when you're around to help.

394
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:37,240
我想念他
I miss him.

395
00:14:38,180 --> 00:14:38,740
我知道
Yeah.

396
00:14:39,620 --> 00:14:41,340
他是你第一个真正意义上的男朋友
He was your first real boyfriend.

397
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:44,300
我一直希望他能出现
I keep expecting him to show up.

398
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:47,920
他以前都是晚上过来 我会偷偷溜出去看他
He used to come by at night, and I'd sneak out to see him.

399
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,340
我知道
Yeah, I know.

400
00:14:50,020 --> 00:14:50,660
你知道吗
You knew?

401
00:14:51,155 --> 00:14:53,885
他开一辆没有消音器的三十年前的旧车
His car is 30 years old and doesn't have a muffler.

402
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:55,940
他居然还按喇叭
And he honked.

403
00:14:58,060 --> 00:14:59,460
我超爱那台车
I loved that car.

404
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:01,060
我知道你现在很难过 宝贝
I know it hurts now, sweetheart,

405
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:05,420
但这样你才明白这段感情是值得拥有的
but that's how you know it was a relationship worth having.

406
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:14,200
后来呢
Well, what happened?

407
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:15,600
他回来了吗
Did he come back?

408
00:15:15,832 --> 00:15:16,603
那
That --

409
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:18,740
那就是你 老兄
That was you, buddy.

410
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:21,140
我喜欢这个孩子
I love this kid.

411
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:22,980
我记得他还是个宝宝的时候
I remember when he was a baby.

412
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:26,280
咱们第一次见时我上高中
We met my senior year of high school.

413
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:27,960
大家到底以为我是谁啊
Who does everyone think I am?

414
00:15:28,004 --> 00:15:29,015
你知道
You know, it's --

415
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:32,860
有关宝宝 你爱上一个宝宝
Thing about babies, you -- you fall in love with a baby

416
00:15:32,934 --> 00:15:35,040
胖嘟嘟超级可爱
with the cutest little fat folds,

417
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:37,320
然后 突然 他们就离开了
and then -- bam -- they're gone.

418
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:38,800
但没事 因为取而代之的
But it's okay, because in its place

419
00:15:39,551 --> 00:15:42,000
是个学步的娃娃
is this...toddler

420
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,080
拥有世上最美好的笑声
with the greatest laugh on Earth.

421
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:46,280
然后又一天 这个娃娃也不见了
And then one day, the toddler's gone,

422
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:48,240
取代的 是一个小孩子
and in its place, a little kid

423
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:52,080
他会问你听过的最有趣的问题
that asks the most interesting questions you've ever heard.

424
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:54,020
就一直这样子
And this keeps going on like that,

425
00:15:54,100 --> 00:15:56,690
但你从没有错过他们的机会
but you never get the chance to miss any of them,

426
00:15:56,690 --> 00:15:59,884
因为总会有一个新的孩子取代之前那个
'cause there's always a new kid to take the place of the old.

427
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:01,720
直到他们长大
Until they grow up.

428
00:16:01,954 --> 00:16:05,280
然后 突然
And then...in a moment,

429
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:07,440
所有这些你爱上的孩子们
all those kids you fell in love with

430
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:10,920
同时走出了家门
walk out the door at the same time.

431
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:12,260
天啊
Jesus.

432
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:14,200
我不是故意扫兴
Oh, I don't mean to be a bummer.

433
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:16,020
我只是说 时光飞逝
I'm just saying it goes fast.

434
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:17,820
就像老话说的
Like the expression...

435
00:16:19,160 --> 00:16:21,060
"你永远不知道最后一次抱起自己孩子是什么时候"
"You never know the last time you pick up your kid."

436
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:22,940
海莉 我们要说的是
The point we're making, Haley,

437
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:25,521
担心自己的孩子很正常
is that it's natural to worry over your kids.

438
00:16:25,521 --> 00:16:27,233
说明你爱他们
It -- It just means that you love them.

439
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:29,880
所以我一直会感觉我把他们养坏了
So, I'm always gonna feel like I screwed them up somehow?

440
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:31,420
差不多
Kind of.

441
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:33,720
但最终你能够一笑而过
I mean, eventually, you'll be able to laugh at it --

442
00:16:33,780 --> 00:16:36,800
大概是你向自己孩子保证
probably around the time that you're reassuring your own children

443
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:38,300
他们没有养坏他们宝宝的时候吧
that they didn't screw up their babies.

444
00:16:39,420 --> 00:16:39,940
谢谢啦
Thanks.

445
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:41,720
不 谢谢你
No, actually, thank you.

446
00:16:42,299 --> 00:16:45,160
作为父母 我们很高兴知道我们仍有
It's nice to know, as parents, that we can still have --

447
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:45,480
爸爸
Dad?

448
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:47,820
我想念抱起我的小女儿
I miss picking up my little girl.

449
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:49,940
不会是最后一次的 可恶
And it won't be the last time, damn it!

450
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,004
你想要我骑在我肩上吗 宝贝
Oh! You want a piggyback ride, honey?

451
00:16:52,004 --> 00:16:52,954
不不不
No. No. No.

452
00:16:52,954 --> 00:16:54,220
-你确定 -好了 到此为止
- You sure? - Okay, I'm calling it.

453
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:54,960
天啊
Oh, my gosh!

454
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:56,300
好了 终于来了
Okay, this is it!

455
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:57,840
你好
Hello?

456
00:17:00,860 --> 00:17:02,836
-炸薯条味道很普通啊 -抱歉
- The French fries were only okay. - Sorry about that.

457
00:17:02,904 --> 00:17:05,221
花了点时间才把杰弄上车
Took a minute getting Jay to his car. Mm.

458
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:07,480
他看到一片形状与他以前橄榄球教练相似的云
He saw a cloud that looked like his old football coach,

459
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:08,600
然后他不想自己待着
and he didn't want to be alone.

460
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:11,860
-今晚意外地挺耐人寻味的啊 -是啊
- Turned out to be kind of a fun night, huh? - Yeah.

461
00:17:12,270 --> 00:17:13,263
是的
Yeah.

462
00:17:13,820 --> 00:17:15,000
对了
By the way...

463
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:18,360
我在网上贴的广告收到回复啦
I got a response to my Craigslist ad.

464
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:20,320
那好快啊
Oh. Oh, that was fast.

465
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:20,920
是的
Yeah.

466
00:17:21,360 --> 00:17:23,140
一对人很好的夫妇
Yeah, really nice couple,

467
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:24,900
很快要成为空巢老人
soon to be empty nesters --

468
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:27,398
有3个孩子 2个新生的外孙
three kids, two new grandkids.

469
00:17:27,398 --> 00:17:29,420
老婆有点神经兮兮
Wife's a little high-strung.

470
00:17:29,420 --> 00:17:31,300
老公有点古里古怪
Husband's a bit of an oddball

471
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:33,160
而且对生活十分有激情
with an infectious lust for life.

472
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:35,020
他们听起来好奇怪啊 不卖
They sound like weirdos. No sale.

473
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:36,580
菲尔 我是在说我们俩
Phil, I'm talking about us.

474
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:38,140
我们应该把房车留下
We should keep the RV.

475
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:39,420
这主意真是太棒了
That is amazing.

476
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,480
是什么让你改变了心意
What changed your mind?

477
00:17:41,970 --> 00:17:45,083
我想应该是因为今晚听到的那些故事吧
I think it was hearing all those stories tonight.

478
00:17:45,703 --> 00:17:47,260
孩子们很快就会离我们而去
And the kids'll be gone soon.

479
00:17:47,260 --> 00:17:49,000
我们估计会花很多时间在旅游上
We'll probably spend a lot of time on the road.

480
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:51,680
反正都要出游 何不在极尽奢华
Might as well do it in the height of luxury --

481
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:55,540
带地毯洗手间与四合一游戏桌的车上游呢
with a carpeted bathroom and a four-in-one game table.

482
00:17:55,760 --> 00:17:56,480
你真是太棒了
You're incredible.

483
00:17:56,940 --> 00:17:59,440
我是做了什么好事才能够有你这样的贤妻
What did I do to deserve a wife cool enough

484
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:02,020
让我留下我爸的房车以及他的新生鹦鹉
to let me keep my dad's RV and his newborn parrot?

485
00:18:02,940 --> 00:18:03,800
他的新生什么
His newborn what?

486
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:07,406
亲爱的 鹦鹉的寿命可以到70至8...
Honey, parrots live like 70 to 8-- Mmmmmm.

487
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:15,780
完全没想到会接到的电话啊
That was not the call I was expecting.

488
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:17,910
亲爱的 我懂
Sweetie, I know.

489
00:18:17,910 --> 00:18:20,472
我看到另一个教练在网上发庆祝的照片了
I-I saw the other coach celebrating on Instagram,

490
00:18:20,472 --> 00:18:23,320
浑身都倒了运动饮料 还是在房子里
uh, drenching himself in Gatorade -- in the house.

491
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:25,280
还有地毯呢 谁来清理呢
There was a rug. Who's gonna clean that up?

492
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:26,280
我猜肯定不是他来清理
Not him, I bet.

493
00:18:26,780 --> 00:18:27,880
从你的表情来看
I'm reading from your face

494
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:29,140
我跟你说之前你是不知道这事的
that you didn't know until I just told you.

495
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:30,400
我现在是紧张所以说个不停
Now I'm just talking out of nerves.

496
00:18:30,660 --> 00:18:32,020
妈的 我...
Damn it! I --

497
00:18:32,020 --> 00:18:33,620
我没被选吗
I didn't get it?!

498
00:18:33,860 --> 00:18:37,259
我知道我喜怒不形于色 但我超想要这工作
I mean, I know I'm hard to read, but I really wanted that job.

499
00:18:37,259 --> 00:18:39,344
我很遗憾 来抱抱
I'm so sorry. C-Come here.

500
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:41,960
等等 所以你才整晚不停跟我说
Wait, is that why you were selling California

501
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:42,980
加州的各种好吗
all night long to me?

502
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:44,980
因为你希望我知道时不会太难过
Because you wanted to soften the blow when I heard?

503
00:18:45,820 --> 00:18:47,060
真是又怪又有点甜
Well, that is weirdly sweet.

504
00:18:47,687 --> 00:18:49,516
-我很快就过来 -好
- I'll be there in a second. - Okay.

505
00:18:50,260 --> 00:18:53,239
我想跟你们说驴子的故事超成功
Um... Just wanted to let you know the donkey story killed.

506
00:18:53,239 --> 00:18:55,400
-哈哈 -一下让场面不再尴尬
- Ha ha! - It totally broke the ice.

507
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:56,520
我们聊得非常开心
We've been having so much fun!

508
00:18:56,600 --> 00:18:57,900
宝贝 我好为你开心
Oh, honey! I'm so happy!

509
00:18:58,160 --> 00:18:58,920
谢谢 我也很开心
Thanks. Me, too.

510
00:18:58,929 --> 00:19:01,105
他问我能不能去外面一起吃个冰激凌
He asked if I could go outside and get ice cream.

511
00:19:01,220 --> 00:19:01,915
我可以去吗
Can I?

512
00:19:01,915 --> 00:19:03,200
当然啦 没问题
O-Of course, yes.

513
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:05,720
但选择配料时要非常谨慎
But just make good choices about the toppings.

514
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:08,020
不要加糖屑 那是蜡做的垃圾
Don't get sprinkles. They're just wax.

515
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:12,720
至少我们也获得了一个小胜利不是吗
Well, now, there's a small victory at least, right?

516
00:19:12,940 --> 00:19:15,798
初次约会大成功 我们也得到了一次助攻
First date was a success, and we get an assist.

517
00:19:15,798 --> 00:19:17,473
抱歉 我用了橄榄球的术语
S-- Uh, sorry -- football term.

518
00:19:17,473 --> 00:19:18,880
并不是好吗
Eh, except it isn't.

519
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:20,660
对了 你接到的电话是谁打来的
Uh, by the way, what was that phone call you got?

520
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:22,480
简直要疯
Oh. Uh crazy.

521
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:24,960
是我们的领养中介
Our adoption agency.

522
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:25,878
很多年以前的那个吗
From years ago?

523
00:19:25,878 --> 00:19:29,780
对啊 他们最近在搬移数据库
Y-Yeah, apparently, uh, they were migrating the database,

524
00:19:29,780 --> 00:19:33,640
我们的档案意外被重启了 然后呢...
and somehow, our profile got accidentally reactivated and --

525
00:19:34,009 --> 00:19:35,260
有人选了我们
and somebody picked us.

526
00:19:35,260 --> 00:19:36,340
等等 选我们
Wait, picked us?

527
00:19:36,591 --> 00:19:38,700
是指给我们小宝宝吗
A-As in there-- there's a baby?

528
00:19:38,700 --> 00:19:39,780
对啊 是不是太疯狂了
I know. Wild, right?

529
00:19:39,790 --> 00:19:41,920
那你... 你拒绝他们了吧
W-Well, you -- you told them no?

530
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:44,241
我觉得不跟你说就拒绝不太好
Well, it felt wrong until I talked to you about it,

531
00:19:44,241 --> 00:19:46,201
但 我... 我会
but, yeah, I-I'll -- I will.

532
00:19:46,201 --> 00:19:47,060
我会跟他们说的
I'll tell 'em.

533
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:51,020
今晚说那些故事真是很有趣呢
It was really fun telling those stories tonight.

534
00:19:51,020 --> 00:19:51,620
对啊
Yeah.

535
00:19:51,980 --> 00:19:54,060
让我换了一个角度来看待失去工作这件事
Really puts losing a job in perspective.

536
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:55,580
我们人生最好的那些回忆
You know, none of our best memories

537
00:19:55,580 --> 00:19:56,960
跟工作完全没有任何关系
have anything to do with work.

538
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:00,020
反而全都是跟外面那个小姑娘有关
They all have to do with that little girl right out there.

539
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:02,360
你知道其实她也已经不小了吧
Well, you know, she's not so little anymore.

540
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:06,040
感觉牵手的时刻要到了
Oh. Oh, I think we're about to have a hand-holding moment.

541
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:12,880
我们这些年来对养孩子也十分有心得了吧
You know, we got pretty good at this parenting thing,

542
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:13,380
你觉得呢
didn't we?

543
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:20,120
我们今晚就得回复那个中介吗
so, uh, we -- we have to tell the agency tonight?

544
00:20:22,081 --> 00:20:27,185
我们应该有24小时的时间可以做决定
Well, technically, we have 24 hours to, uh...decide.

545
00:20:27,185 --> 00:20:28,129
好的
Okay.

546
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:37,520
杰
Jay.

547
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:38,780
对不起
I'm sorry.

548
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:40,980
我以后不会再给你下药了
I will never drug you again.

549
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:43,820
但是看到你吐露心事与诚实真的很好呢
But it was so nice to see you so open and honest.

550
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:45,800
我也当了一回"正直的亚伯"了
Yeah, I was a regular "Honest Abe."

551
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:46,840
那是谁啊
Who's that?

552
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:51,040
偶尔释放一下感情或许也是件好事吧
It's probably good to be emotional every now and then.

553
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:54,220
或许我该练习练习不吃药就能做到那样
I should probably practice letting it out without a pill.

554
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:57,240
我很为你的表演感到骄傲呢
Hey, I was proud of you in that show you did.

555
00:20:57,480 --> 00:20:58,520
我爱你
I love you!

556
00:20:58,580 --> 00:21:01,340
我知道 同样的对话我们昨晚说过四次了
I know. We had this conversation four times last night.

557
00:21:01,420 --> 00:21:01,740
真的吗
Really?

558
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:05,100
或许你该检查一下你都打给谁过
Um, maybe you should check your call history.

559
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:08,460
别啊
Oh, no.

560
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:11,120
你激励了我
You inspire me.

561
00:21:11,260 --> 00:21:13,180
菲尔 或许就是因为那样
And I think I'm rude to you sometimes

562
00:21:13,180 --> 00:21:15,020
所以我有时候会故意对你不太有礼
because I'm scared of that, Phil.

563
00:21:15,020 --> 00:21:16,420
这是我绕着弯在说
This is a long way of saying

564
00:21:16,820 --> 00:21:18,780
我想我终于有了最好的死党
I think I finally have a best friend.

565
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:21,620
你激励了我
You inspire me.

566
00:21:22,260 --> 00:21:23,560
菲尔 或许就是因为那样
And I think I'm rude to you sometimes
